      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GREAT COSMIC (1) is a former NSW galloper who has started four times for the new yard and been far too good all four. Has a big weight but racing in great confidence and looks hard to beat again. DEFERENTIAL (2) looks the biggest danger. Was a strong winner fresh off a long break and will only strip fitter. Looks very hard to stop again. FRAWLEY (5) was in the placings when a length back from the winner last start at Mt Isa and is down in weight this time. Sure to go close if runs up to the mark. IOANE (3) was never in contention when resuming last start over 1400m at Morphettville Parks, finishing ninth and beaten 6 lengths. Showed good speed there and swamped late. First run for the new yard and can give a sight this level. STECARA (4) is capable of more than she showed last time.",
